  "note": "Aptos (M365 default body face since 2023): Word renders the real font, but\nit ships only inside Office, so Chromium never resolves it and the chain\nfell to Carlito, 5% narrower per line, one line short per paragraph (SAS\nprobe 2026-09-03: seven samples, pitch stays Calibri's 1.22). Aptos is not\na scale of Carlito: per glyph the ratio spans 0.87 (M, t, r) to 1.22 (C, s,\nc), so one factor fitted over whole lines left capitals 2.7% and bold 1.3%\nshort and moved a wrap every two pages (prod corpus 2026-10-20). Each face\ntherefore declares the corpus-weighted letter scale as its general rule and\none range-limited face per 1.5% advance bucket of the ASCII letters, digits,\nspace and common punctuation; later faces win inside their unicode-range.\nRatios = Aptos hmtx (Word DFonts / cloud-font cache) over Carlito hmtx,\ntimes the face's mean pair-kerning factor (0.9957-0.9963 over the corpus):\nWord kerns every run under the 2024 Normal template (docDefaults kern 2)\nand HarfBuzz kern+liga reproduces its PDF line widths exactly, while\nChromium cannot kern across the bucket faces. The metric overrides undo\neach face's size-adjust on the vertical axis (overrides scale with\nsize-adjust) so every bucket carries the line box of the 106.5% Carlito\nface the pagination model (line-metrics.ts) assumes: a 1.22x capital\nbucket otherwise grew a 12pt body line 0.4pt. Generated: do not hand-edit\nthe numbers, refit them against the font files.",
